# Workflow Observability Spine

Joel refinement, 2026-06-04: this is not primarily about the HUD. The visualizer is one consumer. The real thing is the **observability spine under the hood**: structured telemetry, traces, events, cost/token/sandbox accounting, and agent-readable receipts that let humans and agents understand a workflow while it runs and after it finishes.

Agent observability may be more important than the eyeball UI. A debugging agent should be able to attach to a run, inspect the telemetry pack, and explain what is right, what is wrong, what remains, what is costing money, and what the next safe action is.

## Core stance

Observability is not a dashboard bolted on later. It is part of the workflow contract and data model.

## Current App Status — 2026-06-09

The production app now has a **runtime receipt/audit spine**, but not the full observability/telemetry spine described here.

What exists in `src/app`:

- `WorkflowRunResult.eventLog` records typed safety-envelope state transitions with timestamps, summaries, and artifact refs.
- The capsule supervisor appends events by `workItemId`, so the Durable Object can preserve run/capsule history.
- The Cloudflare status projection now mirrors each transition to D1 `workflow_events` keyed by `(run_id, event_index)`. `GET /runs/:runId/events` returns a typed redacted `workflow.event-stream.v1` JSON snapshot, `Accept: text/event-stream` or `?format=sse` returns a Server-Sent Events replay, and `?tail=live` / `?live=1` returns bounded live-tail SSE with `after` or `Last-Event-ID` resume support plus typed `workflow.event-tail-control.v1` close events. This is an event projection/observer route, not a full debugger attach surface.
- Pi planner/worker/verifier lane receipts record runtime, `realAgent`, sandbox ref, prompt ref, transcript ref, output pins, receipt ref, Artifacts commit SHA, redacted `AgentAuthLease`, redacted `WorkflowTraceContext`, and sandbox accounting cleanup/duration metadata when backed by the Cloudflare Sandbox runtime. Production-mode real-agent receipts are invalid without propagated trace context.
- Deterministic verification is now a real port path, not a decorative schema branch. `createArtifactEvidenceDeterministicVerifier` runs only for contracts selecting `builtin:artifact-evidence-integrity.v1`; it blocks unknown checks, validates pinned evidence hashes, requires worker evidence and the observability pack, checks declared side effects against capability receipts, and writes `workflow.verification-result.v1` at the contract output path. Default real runs still use Pi verifier lanes unless the plan selects this deterministic source.
- Capability lease and execution receipts record actor/resource/payload-hash/review-gate/secret-ref boundaries plus redacted `WorkflowTraceContext`; dry-run still leases. Local integration coverage now proves issued leases, broker-recorded execution receipts, and capability structured logs preserve the requested side-effect span.
- Discord message delivery now has both dry-run and real send paths behind the same `discord.message.send` lease. The real adapter requires a typed `workflow.discord-message-approval.v1` review gate approval, trusted secret ref, adapter-local token materialization, and pinned payload hash verification before calling Discord.
- Wzrrd review-surface delivery now has both dry-run and real publisher paths behind the same `wzrrd.site.publish` lease. The real adapter requires a typed `workflow.wzrrd-publish-approval.v1` review gate approval, trusted secret ref, adapter-local token materialization, and pinned review-surface hash verification before publishing to Wzrrd.
- GitHub PR review-surface delivery now has dry-run and real adapter paths behind two explicit operations: `github.branch.commit` and `github.pull-request.create`. The app writes typed `github.branch-commit-payload.v1` plus `github.pull-request-payload.v1` artifacts for `outputTarget.kind === "github-pr"`, requests payload-hash-bound leases, executes `GitHubBranchCommitCapabilityAdapter` before `GitHubPullRequestCapabilityAdapter`, and records both capability receipts through the broker. The real branch adapter requires an approved non-dry-run lease, trusted GitHub branch secret ref, adapter-local token materialization, repository/base/head binding, pinned payload hash verification, per-file content hashes, safe repository paths, and GitHub refs/trees/commits writes. The real PR adapter requires an approved non-dry-run lease, trusted GitHub PR secret ref, adapter-local token materialization, repository/base/head resource binding, and pinned payload hash verification before calling GitHub's create-pull-request API. Live receipt `run-live-github-pr-dryrun-20260609T060703Z-9bba1f11` proved deployed main-app dry-run PR delivery through real Pi planner/worker/verifier lanes before this branch-commit lease was added. Live receipt `run-live-github-branch-pr-20260609T065340Z-f82a6d90` proved deployed non-dry-run branch+PR delivery through real Pi planner/worker/verifier lanes, executed `github.branch.commit`, executed `github.pull-request.create`, committed `2b67364fd7435e64b1916c5a68b768ceb48605ea`, and opened `https://github.com/joelhooks/pi-cloudflare-sandbox-workflows/pull/16`.
- Linear comment review-surface delivery now has dry-run and real adapter paths behind `linear.comment.create`. The app writes typed `linear.comment-payload.v1` artifacts for `outputTarget.kind === "linear"`, requests payload-hash-bound leases on `linear.issue:<issueRef>`, executes a `LinearCommentCapabilityAdapter`, and records the capability receipt through the broker. The real adapter requires an approved non-dry-run lease, trusted Linear secret ref, adapter-local token materialization, Linear GraphQL issue lookup by id/key, body hash verification, and pinned payload hash/resource binding before calling `commentCreate`. Integration tests cover the adapter, D1 broker persistence, app dry-run path, app approved path, and real planner prompt contract. Live deployed dry-run receipt `run-live-linear-dryrun-20260609T072514Z-fee16d9c` proved this path through real Pi planner/worker/verifier lanes with final review surface kind `linear`, dry-run `linear.comment.create` on `linear.issue:PIWF-123`, a D1 `linear` receipt row, and `31` telemetry rows. Live non-dry-run Linear proof still needs a configured Linear token and target issue.
- Review summary and review surface artifacts include the event log, plan/machine/harness refs, package refs, lane receipts, verifier result, capability receipts, and redacted artifact refs.
- `workflow.review-surface.v1` now includes a typed `definitionOfDone.observability` requirement. It makes runtime observability, telemetry, structured high-cardinality logs, trace spans, metrics, token/cost/sandbox accounting, capability-lease receipts, an agent-readable observability pack, and a strict redaction policy machine-readable acceptance evidence.
- `workflow.review-surface.v1` now also includes `definitionOfDone.workflowChain`, a typed completion-chain audit for the real execution path. It marks intent/policy, capsule, package pinning, real Pi planner, pinned plan artifacts, real Pi worker lanes, capability leases, verifier result, review surface, and captured receipts independently. Verification may be a real Pi verifier lane or a plan-selected deterministic verifier result; integration-test/memory lanes and verifier bypasses stay incomplete.
- `workflow.review-surface.v1` now also includes `definitionOfDone.reconciliation`, a typed proposal reconciliation audit for configured Wzrrd acceptance refs. It marks package-first primitive, Artifact-backed package pinning, entitlement/trust policy, generated XState workflow, real Pi lanes, capability-leased side effects, receipt-backed review surface, and observability/redaction envelope independently. Local integration proof keeps integration-test lanes `linked` with missing proposal requirements and lets the front-door real-lane-shaped composition reach `reconciled`. Live receipt `run-live-proposal-reconciliation-20260609T085022Z-9810b18a` proved the deployed public review surface reaches `definitionOfDone.reconciliation.status=reconciled`, with eight captured proposal requirements and no missing workflow-chain IDs.
- `workflow.observability-pack.v1` now exists as a first production-intended artifact written at `run/observability-pack.json` before verifier execution. It is emitted through the required `WorkflowObservabilityRecorderPort`; `createCloudflareArtifactsObservabilityRecorder` is the Artifact-backed production-intended adapter wired by the Cloudflare front door. The pack contains redacted structured log records, required high-cardinality field names, run metrics, artifact refs, lane receipt refs, capability receipt refs, sandbox accounting status/duration metrics when real lane receipts provide them, structured telemetry sink receipts, token/cost accounting status plus aggregate `tokenCount`/`tokenCostEstimate` metrics when lane receipts carry explicit accounting, and trace propagation status plus structured span counts when lane and capability receipts carry propagated trace context.
- Trace propagation progress: `AgentLaneRuntimeRequest` now carries `traceContext`; Cloudflare Pi planner/worker/verifier adapters derive deterministic trace/span IDs from the run/lane; the Cloudflare Sandbox Pi command exposes `WORKFLOW_TRACE_ID`, `WORKFLOW_SPAN_ID`, and `WORKFLOW_TRACE_CONTEXT_JSON`; committed lane receipts persist that context; and lane structured logs use the receipt span ID instead of a recorder-invented lane span. Capability lease requests, issued leases, and execution receipts now require `traceContext`; `WorkflowApp` derives deterministic side-effect spans for dynamic Discord steps and review-surface delivery operations, and the observability recorder uses those receipt spans in `workflow.capability.receipt` logs. Integration coverage proves front-door real-lane-shaped composition reaches `metrics.tracePropagationStatus=captured` only when included lane and capability receipts are traced. Live receipt `run-live-trace-propagation-20260609T091147Z-7fdc512f` on Worker version `00f9f6fd-426c-42f0-9e24-3860aab144f9` proved the deployed lane-trace path before capability receipt spans were added: public review URL `https://run-live-trace-propagation-20260609t091147z-7fdc512f.wzrrd.sh/`, public JSON includes planner/worker/verifier lane `traceContext`, D1 telemetry has `31` rows, `1` trace, and `31` spans, and the fetched observability pack records `metrics.tracePropagationStatus=captured` plus `metrics.traceSpanCount=31`. Live receipt `run-live-capability-trace-20260609T093229Z-eca60175` on Worker version `5b813670-0b3f-4ec4-8d9f-7a2c6810d3f2` proved capability receipt spans in the deployed path: public URL `https://run-live-capability-trace-20260609t093229z-eca60175.wzrrd.sh/`, public JSON includes the `discord.message.send` capability `traceContext`, D1 telemetry has a `workflow.capability.receipt` row using the Discord capability span, the fetched observability pack records `metrics.tracePropagationStatus=captured`, and the fetched post-verifier Wzrrd capability receipt carries its own propagated span.
- `AgentLaneReceipt` now supports optional redacted `tokenCostAccounting`. The Cloudflare Sandbox Pi lane adapter parses explicit usage/cost metadata from Pi stdout/stderr into that receipt field, and the observability recorder projects it into per-lane structured log `tokenCount`/`costEstimate` fields. Local integration coverage proves the pack switches to `captured` when every included lane receipt carries token count and cost data. Live proof `run-live-token-cost-accounting-20260609T083009Z-634cb024` on Worker version `7ce6e4ab-1e05-446c-8805-95d0156d8899` captured the deployed path through real Pi planner/worker/verifier lanes, but the fetched observability pack reports `metrics.tokenCostAccountingStatus=not-yet-instrumented`, `metrics.tokenCount=null`, and `metrics.tokenCostEstimate=null` because Pi emitted no numeric usage/cost metadata.
- `WorkflowTelemetrySinkPort` is now a first-class app port. The Cloudflare front door uses a composite sink: `createCloudflareArtifactsStructuredLogSink` writes `run/telemetry/structured-logs.jsonl`, `createCloudflareD1WorkflowTelemetrySink` writes queryable high-cardinality rows to D1 `workflow_telemetry_logs`, and `createCloudflareAnalyticsEngineWorkflowTelemetrySink` exports bounded Workers Analytics Engine data points when the Worker `WORKFLOW_TELEMETRY` binding exists. Migration `0002_workflow_telemetry_logs.sql` is applied remotely. Live receipt `run-live-analytics-engine-telemetry-20260609T075635Z-ebf7ce3a` proved all three sinks through deployed Worker version `d3e58e38-aaf6-48d0-a74b-58dadff2b97a`: the observability pack contains `31` logs and captured sink receipts for `artifact-jsonl`, `cloudflare-d1-structured-logs`, and `cloudflare-analytics-engine` dataset `pi_cloudflare_sandbox_workflows_telemetry`.
- Event stream live proof: `run-live-event-stream-capture-20260609T100200Z-ee603257` captured through deployed Worker version `0faf4e33-34d8-4e8b-9169-c93033c62d52` after remote migration `0003_workflow_events.sql`. Event route `https://pi-cloudflare-sandbox-workflows.joelhooks.workers.dev/runs/run-live-event-stream-capture-20260609T100200Z-ee603257/events` returned `workflow.event-stream.v1` with `20` events, first state `resolvingCapsule`, final `captured`, and D1 sink metadata. SSE replay returned `text/event-stream` with `workflow.event` and `workflow.snapshot`. Poll receipts prove it advanced during the in-flight POST. Public review URL: `https://run-live-event-stream-capture-20260609t100200z-ee603257.wzrrd.sh/`; Discord message id `1513846203446464604`; D1 telemetry rows `31`, one trace, and `31` spans.
- Event live-tail proof: `run-live-event-tail-capture-20260609T102116Z-e1db65c8` captured through deployed Worker version `749ae924-c5ed-47df-a772-c86167a7a4be`. Event route `https://pi-cloudflare-sandbox-workflows.joelhooks.workers.dev/runs/run-live-event-tail-capture-20260609T102116Z-e1db65c8/events` returned `workflow.event-stream.v1` with `20` events, first state `resolvingCapsule`, final `captured`, and D1 sink metadata. First live-tail SSE receipt `.wrangler/workflow-app/live-runs/run-live-event-tail-capture-20260609T102116Z-e1db65c8-events-live-tail.sse` emitted `workflow.event` ids `1..5` while `POST /runs` was still in flight and then closed with `workflow.tail.closed reason=max-polls`; terminal-tail receipt `.wrangler/workflow-app/live-runs/run-live-event-tail-capture-20260609T102116Z-e1db65c8-events-terminal-tail.sse` resumed after id `5`, emitted ids `6..20`, and closed with `workflow.tail.closed reason=terminal-state`. Public review URL: `https://run-live-event-tail-capture-20260609t102116z-e1db65c8.wzrrd.sh/`; public JSON `https://run-live-event-tail-capture-20260609t102116z-e1db65c8.wzrrd.sh/review-surface.json`; Discord message id `1513851033913393233`; Wzrrd delivery `published`; D1 telemetry rows `31`, one trace, and `31` spans. Preceding proof `run-live-event-tail-20260609T101723Z-bfac4bb6` correctly blocked because the prompt asked the in-run verifier to prove an external observer SSE receipt it could not read; observer proofs should remain external receipts or be pinned as explicit verifier evidence before verification.
- Live receipt `run-live-completion-audit-20260609T051456Z-ad79438e` proved the audit spine plus real Discord send and public Wzrrd review-surface publication through real Pi planner/worker/verifier lanes, non-dry-run `discord.message.send` and `wzrrd.site.publish` capability receipts, public JSON `definitionOfDone.workflowChain.status=captured`, ten captured workflow-chain requirements, Discord message id `1513773945588027504`, and public URL `https://run-live-completion-audit-20260609t051456z-ad79438e.wzrrd.sh/`.
- Live receipt `run-live-telemetry-sinks-20260609T053840Z-4ed6621e` proved the structured telemetry sink spine through the deployed Worker version `1dc7d802-7593-4dad-887f-b7b4b60b2437`: public JSON includes `run/telemetry/structured-logs.jsonl`; remote D1 query returned `31` `workflow_telemetry_logs` rows, one trace id, and span rows for workflow state/status projection events; verifier accepted after `telemetrySinks` extraction was added to the Pi verifier prompt evidence.
- Live receipt `run-live-analytics-engine-telemetry-20260609T075635Z-ebf7ce3a` proved the deployed Workers Analytics Engine sink through Worker version `d3e58e38-aaf6-48d0-a74b-58dadff2b97a`: public review URL `https://run-live-analytics-engine-telemetry-20260609t075635z-ebf7ce3a.wzrrd.sh/`, public JSON `https://run-live-analytics-engine-telemetry-20260609t075635z-ebf7ce3a.wzrrd.sh/review-surface.json`, fetched pack `.wrangler/workflow-app/live-runs/run-live-analytics-engine-telemetry-20260609T075635Z-ebf7ce3a-observability-pack.json`, `31` structured logs, `metrics.structuredLogSinkStatus=captured`, D1 query `31` rows and one trace id, non-dry-run Discord message id `1513814825799520388`, non-dry-run Wzrrd delivery `published`, and telemetry sink receipts for `artifact-jsonl`, `cloudflare-d1-structured-logs`, and `cloudflare-analytics-engine` with dataset `pi_cloudflare_sandbox_workflows_telemetry`.
- Live receipt `run-live-token-cost-accounting-20260609T083009Z-634cb024` proved the deployed token/cost plumbing path through Worker version `7ce6e4ab-1e05-446c-8805-95d0156d8899`: public review URL `https://run-live-token-cost-accounting-20260609t083009z-634cb024.wzrrd.sh/`, public JSON `https://run-live-token-cost-accounting-20260609t083009z-634cb024.wzrrd.sh/review-surface.json`, fetched pack `.wrangler/workflow-app/live-runs/run-live-token-cost-accounting-20260609T083009Z-634cb024-observability-pack.json`, `31` structured logs, D1 query `31` rows and one trace id, non-dry-run Discord message id `1513823271773274234`, non-dry-run Wzrrd delivery `published`, `metrics.tokenCostAccountingStatus=not-yet-instrumented`, `metrics.tokenCount=null`, and `metrics.tokenCostEstimate=null`. This is an honest live non-capture receipt, not a captured token bill.

What does **not** exist yet:

- deeper child spans inside the broker, review-surface publisher internals, and external telemetry exporters beyond current structured receipt spans
- live token/cost accounting captured from Pi/provider metadata; retry/cancellation timing; or lane queue latency metrics beyond the current pack status
- true WebSocket observer, public debugger-agent attach surface, or richer run inspection UI beyond the D1 event snapshot/SSE replay/live-tail route
- external telemetry sinks beyond Analytics Engine, such as Axiom, Langfuse, OTEL, or equivalent
- live deployed non-dry-run Linear comment proof and other non-Discord/Wzrrd/GitHub/Linear output adapters

Important framing: the existing receipt chain and `workflowChain` audit are necessary and useful, but they are not enough to call runtime observability “done.” They are replay/audit evidence. The observability spine still needs typed telemetry ports/adapters that let humans and debugging agents inspect a run during execution and after capture.

## Definition Of Done Lock — 2026-06-09

Runtime observability is a definition-of-done gate, not a polish task. A run can have useful receipts and still fail the product DoD if it lacks typed telemetry and structured high-cardinality logs.

The review surface DoD must keep this requirement visible until the app can publish the full observability pack:

```txt
required signals:
  structured-high-cardinality-logs
  runtime-event-log
  trace-spans
  metrics
  cost-token-accounting
  sandbox-accounting
  capability-lease-receipts
  agent-readable-observability-pack
  redaction-policy

required high-cardinality fields:
  runId
  workItemId
  capsuleId
  actorId
  packageId
  packageVersion
  artifactRepo
  artifactRef
  artifactCommitSha
  laneId
  laneKind
  laneRuntime
  sandboxRef
  admissionId
  stepId
  stepKind
  capability
  leaseId
  resourceRef
  payloadHash
  verifierResultId
  reviewSurfaceId
  blockerCode
  traceId
  spanId
  durationMs
  tokenCount
  costEstimate
```

Redaction rule: high cardinality does not mean high leakage. Logs and telemetry must never include raw secrets, raw Pi auth JSON, Discord tokens, claim URLs, token-bearing Artifacts remotes, unredacted private corpus chunks, or broad customer data. Emit stable ids, refs, hashes, and redacted summaries; store bulky or sensitive material only behind explicit artifact refs and policy checks.

